From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Recents: draw transition bitmaps in software without a GPU

PW3 Test V34: opening the recents screen from an application, or an
application from the recents screen, blocks SystemUI's main thread for 24 s
("Long monitor contention with owner main ... ThreadedRenderer
.nCreateHardwareBitmap", RenderThread busy for 16 s) and ends in "System UI
isn't responding". RecentsTransitionHelper.drawViewIntoGraphicBuffer() draws
the task header for the window transition into a hardware bitmap; without a
GPU that is rendered by GLES on the CPU.

When SystemUI's own windows are drawn by the software canvas (every process
is, by patch 0006 and ro.pw3.software_canvas; SystemUI had a switch of its own
until 2026-10-29, when it went as a duplicate), the header is drawn the same
way, straight into the graphic buffer.

--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/recents/views/RecentsTransitionHelper.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/recents/views/RecentsTransitionHelper.java
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@
 import android.graphics.Canvas;
 import android.graphics.Color;
 import android.graphics.GraphicBuffer;
+import android.graphics.PixelFormat;
+import android.graphics.PorterDuff;
 import android.graphics.Rect;
 import android.os.Bundle;
 import android.os.Handler;
@@ -420,6 +422,31 @@
 
     public static GraphicBuffer drawViewIntoGraphicBuffer(int bufferWidth, int bufferHeight,
             View view, float scale, int eraseColor) {
+        if (ThreadedRenderer.sRendererDisabled) {
+            // This process draws its windows with the software canvas: there is
+            // no GPU, a hardware bitmap would be rendered by GLES on the CPU.
+            final GraphicBuffer buffer = GraphicBuffer.create(bufferWidth, bufferHeight,
+                    PixelFormat.RGBA_8888, GraphicBuffer.USAGE_SW_WRITE_RARELY
+                            | GraphicBuffer.USAGE_HW_TEXTURE | GraphicBuffer.USAGE_HW_COMPOSER);
+            if (buffer == null) {
+                return null;
+            }
+            final Canvas canvas = buffer.lockCanvas();
+            if (canvas == null) {
+                buffer.destroy();
+                return null;
+            }
+            canvas.drawColor(Color.TRANSPARENT, PorterDuff.Mode.SRC);
+            canvas.scale(scale, scale);
+            if (eraseColor != 0) {
+                canvas.drawColor(eraseColor);
+            }
+            if (view != null) {
+                view.draw(canvas);
+            }
+            buffer.unlockCanvasAndPost(canvas);
+            return buffer;
+        }
         RenderNode node = RenderNode.create("RecentsTransition", null);
         node.setLeftTopRightBottom(0, 0, bufferWidth, bufferHeight);
         node.setClipToBounds(false);
